Brighter Pocket Companion keeps itself up to date and says what changed.

Sparkle 2 (pinned exactly, through Swift Package Manager) replaces the setup app's own
check, which asked GitHub's API for the latest release and linked to its page. The feed is
an appcast attached to the latest GitHub release (management/Info.plist, an overlay file:
SUFeedURL on releases/latest/download/appcast.xml), each item the release's DMG signed
with the project's EdDSA key; the public half is built in from the build setting
POCKET_SPARKLE_PUBLIC_KEY (tools/make_companion.sh). Without it (a local build, a fork)
updates are off and the app menu says so, rather than checking what it could not verify.
Checks run on Sparkle's schedule and nothing installs without the user's OK; Settings
turns the checks off (the old toggle's state field stays, unused, so saved state still
reads). The app carries CHANGELOG.md (an overlay file) and shows this version's section
once after it updated itself (App/Views/WhatsNew.swift), and from Help. The updater and
the sheet stay off while unit tests host the app. Not an upstream candidate as it stands:
it names Brighter Pocket's repository; Tolkara Management could take the same approach
with its own feed and key.

